{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1491885-aeon-psychic-anima","id":1491885,"title":"[AEON] Psychic Anima","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-30T03:16:38-07:00","id":1491885,"title":"[AEON] Psychic Anima","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I have a small question, how do you deal with the visual effects of Psi powers (the ones not obvious)?<br /> <br /> As I read, psionic powers have no anima, what means you can't tell a Telepath is using his powers, or who is lifting or setting fire on a object. But we see in a few arts some kind of anima (a little ripple in the air, the fire being shot from the hands, etc). Using attunement other psi users are capable of sensing and tracking the powers, but neutrals cant see it.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of psi users eyes shining when using their powers, it gives some supernatural effect to the power and show how hard the character is trying. <br /> <br /> My suggestion is whenever the psi user spends psi, their eyes shine, the more psi spent in an action, the stronger it shines.<br /> Lets say, 1 psi and there is a visible light in the eyes, enough to be seen in the dark, but not the illuminate anything. With 2 Psi spent the shine covers the entire eye. 3 psi and a flame like shine start to flow out of the eyes, and with more psi spent the thicker and brighter it shines.<br /> For daily uses (low dots and no reaching) the result is nothing, but at higher dots, specially when reaching, it would be particularly distinguishable.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T04:33:57-07:00","id":1491888,"title":"","content":"For me, that would be taking away an important advantage of psionic powers. That said, having some kind of visual or environmental quirk due to a high concentration of psi use makes sense to me. How about making it a specific effect for each mode? For example, the light effects you mention would make sense for photokinesis. Then for telepathy, we could have the people around the psion hearing whispers that become louder and louder. Regarding the cost, I'm okay with the escalation, but I would also give the psion an option to keep it subtle: increase the cost, suffer injuries, spend momentun, etc...I can't really think of one right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value"